<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Kiganda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1903">1903</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Kiganda was the agreement of June 1903 by which Mwami <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mwezi-iv-gisabo">Mwezi IV Gisabo</a> of Burundi submitted to German authority after years of resistance and a German punitive campaign. In return the Germans recognised him as ruler, and Burundi was then governed through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indirect-rule">indirect rule</a> as part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-east-africa">German East Africa</a>.</p></div>
